          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Freshworks Cuts 11% of Workforce as AI Reshapes Indian-Founded Software Sector",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "Freshworks, the Indian-founded SaaS giant now headquartered in the US, has announced it will cut approximately 11% of its global workforce as AI tools increasingly automate tasks previously handled by human employees. The company cited the rapid adoption of AI-driven software development and support tools as a structural driver of the restructuring. The cuts signal a broader pattern in the Indian-origin tech industry where AI productivity gains are directly translating into workforce reductions.",
            "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/freshworks-to-cut-11-jobs-as-ai-reshapes-software-sector/article70946330.ece",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
